<title>BRAZIL: BRAZIL SENATE PANEL OKAYS FRANCO AS CENBANK HEAD.</title>
<headline>BRAZIL SENATE PANEL OKAYS FRANCO AS CENBANK HEAD.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Senate Economic Affairs Committee voted to approve Gustavo Franco's nomination as Central Bank president by a 21-6 vote.</p>
<p>The committee's decision must now be ratified by the full Senate in a vote expected to take place next Tuesday.</p>
<p>Franco, until now the Central Bank's Director of Foreign Affairs, was nominated to the senior Central Bank position last week after the current president, Gustavo Loyola, turned in his resignation.</p>
<p>Analysts said the Senate is expected to approve Franco's nomination by a wide margin.</p>
<p>(( -- Michael Christie, Brasilia newsroom 5561 3141193))</p>
